#N D flip-flop (Carlini, Part 2)
#O Nicholas Carlini, 2020
#C A latch set or cleared by the data at each rise of the clock. It stores the right bit at its first two clock edges; from the third, the data changes while its gates read it, and the stored bit breaks up.
